From fc312a27bb3f351e5a839e2ceaffbf2946ef63ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 15:13:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: st: add GENPD_FLAG_NO_STAY_ON flag

Set GENPD_FLAG_NO_STAY_ON so the generic PM domain core may power off an
unused STM32MP domain without waiting for sync_state.

Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I6c507f66baf5af5bb536d9ba594669b5232814a9
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/578960
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/st/stm32mp-pm-domain.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/st/stm32mp-pm-domain.c b/drivers/pmdomain/st/stm32mp-pm-domain.c
index 820f5bf874de..f82c8a41d99f 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/st/stm32mp-pm-domain.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/st/stm32mp-pm-domain.c
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ static int stm32mp_pm_domain_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * Domain based only on PM clk framework, no GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP
 	 * support, the wake-up is handled by power domain of interrupt driver
 	 */
-	pd->flags = GENPD_FLAG_PM_CLK | GENPD_FLAG_IRQ_SAFE;
+	pd->flags = GENPD_FLAG_PM_CLK | GENPD_FLAG_IRQ_SAFE | GENPD_FLAG_NO_STAY_ON;
 
 	ret = pm_genpd_init(pd, NULL, false);
 	if (ret)
-- 
